+### strictSlashes
+
+When set, `/` in a pattern only matches `/` in the file path. On
+Windows platforms, this disables the default behavior of treating
+`\\` as `/` for file path comparison, so a path like `a\\b\\c`
+will not match the pattern `a/b/c`.
+
